    "lem-tdmath-particle-exponential-cutoff": {
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "A1",
          "source": "def-tdmath-stable-power-tempered-particle-model",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Fix a positive integer $d$ and use the Euclidean space $\\mathbb R^d$ with norm\n$\\|x\\|_2=\\sqrt{\\langle x,x\\rangle}$ of [[def-euclidean-inner-product]]. A\npair potential is an even Borel-measurable function\n$\\phi:\\mathbb R^d\\to\\overline{\\mathbb R}$ whose image is contained in\n$\\mathbb R\\cup\\{+\\infty\\}$. Here $\\overline{\\mathbb R}$ is the extended real\nline ([[def-extended-reals]]). Borel measurability means the inverse image of\neach Borel subset of $\\overline{\\mathbb R}$ belongs to the Borel sigma-algebra\ngenerated by open sets in the Euclidean topology on $\\mathbb R^d$\n([[def-borel-sigma-algebra-on-the-extended-real-line]],\n[[def-borel-sigma-algebra]]). Even means $\\phi(-x)=\\phi(x)$. The value\n$+\\infty$ represents a forbidden pair separation. Coordinates and\npotential values are numerical values in fixed reference length and energy\nunits.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
