          "source": "cor-continuous-functions-are-borel-measurable",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice. Let $n,m\\ge1$. Every continuous map\n$f : \\mathbb{R}^n \\to \\mathbb{R}^m$ is Borel measurable in\nthe sense of [[def-borel-and-lebesgue-measurable-function-on-rn]].",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F7",
          "source": "thm-composition-with-borel-functions-preserves-measurability",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $(X,\\mathcal{A})$, $(Y,\\mathcal{B})$, and $(Z,\\mathcal{C})$ be measurable\nspaces. If $f : (X,\\mathcal{A}) \\to (Y,\\mathcal{B})$ is measurable and\n$g : (Y,\\mathcal{B}) \\to (Z,\\mathcal{C})$ is measurable, then\n$g \\circ f : (X,\\mathcal{A}) \\to (Z,\\mathcal{C})$ is measurable.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F7",
          "source": "prop-closure-properties-of-measurable-functions-used-by-the-integral",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $(X,\\mathcal A,\\mu)$ be a measure space.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F7",
          "source": "def-extended-reals",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Fix two objects $-\\infty$ and $+\\infty$, distinct from one another and neither of\nthem a real number ([[def-real-numbers]]), and set",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F7",
          "source": "def-borel-sigma-algebra-on-the-extended-real-line",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "The **extended real line** is",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F7",
          "source": "thm-exponential-is-strictly-increasing",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "The exponential function is continuous and strictly increasing on $\\mathbb R$.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F8",
          "source": "lem-integer-part",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Identify $\\mathbb{Z}$ with its canonical copy inside $\\mathbb{R}$, along the\nembeddings $\\mathbb{N} \\to \\mathbb{Z} \\to \\mathbb{Q} \\to \\mathbb{R}$\n([[lem-nat-embeds-int]], [[lem-int-embeds-rat]], [[lem-rat-embeds-dense]],\n[[def-integers]]). Then for every real $x$ there is **exactly one** integer $m$\nwith",
          "uses": [
            "3.2"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "By [A1] and $\\beta>0$, every configuration satisfies\n$0\\le e^{-\\beta U_N}\\le e^{\\beta BN}$, with the value $0$ when $U_N=+\\infty$.\nFact [F7] makes the integrand and its restriction to $\\Lambda_L^N$\nmeasurable. For every simple minorant of this restricted integrand, [L1]\nbounds its integral by the integral of the constant $e^{\\beta BN}$ on\n$\\Lambda_L^N$.",
          "step": "1.1",
          "inputs": [
            "A1",
            "F1",
            "F7",
            "L1",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-2-1",
          "claim": "The box and product-measure formulas [F2, F3] give\n$\\lambda_d^{\\otimes N}(\\Lambda_L^N)=L^{dN}$. Thus\n$Z_{L,N}\\le(ae^{\\beta B}L^d)^N/N!=(QL^d)^N/N!$ for $N\\ge1$, and this\nalso holds for $N=0$ since $Z_{L,0}=1$.",
          "step": "2.1",
          "inputs": [
            "F2",
            "F3",
            "step 1.1",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-3-1",
          "claim": "Summing the nonnegative terms by [F6] and using [F4] gives\n$1\\le\\Xi_L\\le\\sum_{N=0}^{\\infty}(QL^d)^N/N!=e^{QL^d}$; the lower bound is\nthe empty-configuration term.",
          "step": "3.1",
          "inputs": [
            "F4",
            "F6",
            "step 2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-3-2",
          "claim": "By [F8], $KL^d<n_L\\le KL^d+1$. If $N>n_L$, then $N>KL^d$, so\n$1\\le e^{N-KL^d}$. Therefore\n$$\\sum_{N>n_L}Z_{L,N}\\le e^{-KL^d}\\sum_{N>n_L}\\frac{(eQL^d)^N}{N!}\\le e^{-KL^d}e^{eQL^d}=e^{(eQ-K)L^d}\\le e^{-L^d}.$$\nThe second inequality extends a nonnegative partial tail to the full\nexponential series; the equality uses [F5], and the last inequality follows\nfrom $K>eQ+1$ and [F5].",
          "step": "3.2",
          "inputs": [
            "F4",
            "F5",
            "F8",
            "step 2.1",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-4-1",
          "claim": "For each $M>n_L$, split the $M$th partial sum into the fixed finite prefix\n$\\Xi_L^{\\mathrm{cut}}$ and the finite tail from $n_L+1$ through $M$.\nTaking suprema over $M$ in the nonnegative-series definition [F6] gives\n$\\Xi_L=\\Xi_L^{\\mathrm{cut}}+\\sum_{N>n_L}Z_{L,N}$; subtraction is valid because\nstep 3.1 proves $\\Xi_L<\\infty$. Since $\\Xi_L\\ge1$, step 3.2 implies\n$\\Xi_L^{\\mathrm{cut}}\\ge\\Xi_L-e^{-L^d}\\ge(1-e^{-L^d})\\Xi_L$.",
          "step": "4.1",
          "inputs": [
            "F6",
            "step 3.1",
            "step 3.2",
            "algebra"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "routine_steps": [],
      "boundaries": [
        {
          "case": "empty",
          "status": "checked",
          "evidence": "Steps 2.1 and 3.1 include Z_{L,0}=1, which gives Xi_L≥1."
        },
        {
          "case": "zero",
          "status": "checked",
          "evidence": "Statement N=0 is defined separately by Z_L,0=1 and 0!=1. The factorial denominators are positive integers, a,beta>0, and the cutoff comparison uses L>=1 so 1-exp(-L^d)>0.",
          "case_scope": {
            "source_section": "Statement",
            "source_excerpt": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$\n([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $d\\ge1$, let $\\phi$ be a stable pair\npotential as in [[def-tdmath-stable-power-tempered-particle-model]] with\nstability constant $B$, and fix $a,\\beta>0$. In fixed reference length and\nenergy units, put $\\Lambda_L=[0,L]^d$ and define, for $N\\ge1$,\n$$Z_{L,N}:=\\frac{a^N}{N!}\\int_{\\Lambda_L^N}e^{-\\beta U_N(q_1,\\ldots,q_N)}\\,d\\lambda_d^{\\otimes N},$$\nwhere $\\lambda_d$ is Lebesgue measure restricted to the Borel subsets of\n$\\mathbb R^d$, $\\lambda_d^{\\otimes N}$ is its $N$-fold product measure. The\nintegrand uses the ordinary real exponential when $U_N<+\\infty$ and is defined\nto be $0$ when $U_N=+\\infty$. Also,\n$\\int_{\\Lambda_L^N}f\\,d\\lambda_d^{\\otimes N}$ abbreviates the nonnegative\nintegral of $f\\mathbf1_{\\Lambda_L^N}$ on the full product space, using\n[[def-tdmath-measure-integral]]. Set $Z_{L,0}=1$.\nDefine $\\Xi_L:=\\sum_{N=0}^{\\infty}Z_{L,N}$ as the nonnegative extended sum of\n[[def-nonnegative-extended-series]]. For $L\\ge1$ put\n$Q:=a e^{\\beta B}$. Choose any real $K>eQ+1$ and set\n$$n_L:=\\lfloor K L^d\\rfloor+1.$$\nwhich satisfies $K L^d<n_L\\le K L^d+1$ by the integer-part lemma\n[[lem-integer-part]]. Let\n$\\Xi_L^{\\mathrm{cut}}:=\\sum_{N=0}^{n_L}Z_{L,N}$. Then\n$$1\\le\\Xi_L\\le e^{Q L^d},\\qquad \\sum_{N>n_L}Z_{L,N}\\le e^{-L^d},\\qquad \\Xi_L^{\\mathrm{cut}}\\ge(1-e^{-L^d})\\Xi_L.$$",
            "current_raw_sha256": "3461ed048989450a61f1597c770806ca82a73a04e7ec675e2e09661045e7cf16",
            "scope_only_not_proof_acceptance": true
          }
        },
        {
          "case": "one",
          "status": "checked",
          "evidence": "Steps 2.1 and 3.1 cover N=1 and separately define the N=0 term."
        },
        {
          "case": "degenerate",
          "status": "not_applicable",
          "reason": "No dimension or rank degeneracy is singled out."
        },
        {
