          "status": "current published mathematical supplier; exact interface inspected",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "exact_statement": "Let $(X,\\mathcal{A})$, $(Y,\\mathcal{B})$, and $(Z,\\mathcal{C})$ be measurable\nspaces. If $f : (X,\\mathcal{A}) \\to (Y,\\mathcal{B})$ is measurable and\n$g : (Y,\\mathcal{B}) \\to (Z,\\mathcal{C})$ is measurable, then\n$g \\circ f : (X,\\mathcal{A}) \\to (Z,\\mathcal{C})$ is measurable.",
