          "status": "current published mathematical supplier; exact interface inspected",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "exact_statement": "For $x\\in\\mathbb R$, define\n$$\\exp(x):=\\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty}\\frac{x^n}{\\iota(n!)}, \\qquad e:=\\exp(1),$$\nprovided by the all-real convergence proved in [[lem-exponential-series-has-infinite-radius]]. Here $n!\\in\\mathbb N$ is the factorial of [[def-factorial-and-falling-factorial]], $\\iota(n!)$ is its nonzero real image ([[def-canonical-natural]], [[lem-of-naturals-positive]]), and powers and series are those of [[def-integer-power]] and [[def-series]].",
          "relevant_hypotheses_and_conventions": "The exact excerpt is quoted above; the consumer Facts and proof step state the hypotheses and conventions used.",
          "supplier_proof_status": "Published definition; no proof obligation.",
          "consumer_use": "F4 is used in step(s) 3.1, 3.2."
        },
        {
          "supplier": "lem-exponential-series-has-infinite-radius",
          "carrier": "items/lem-exponential-series-has-infinite-radius.md",
          "status": "current published mathematical supplier; exact interface inspected",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "exact_statement": "For every real $x$, the series $\\sum_{n\\ge0}x^n/\\iota(n!)$ converges absolutely. Its power-series radius is therefore $+\\infty$.",
          "relevant_hypotheses_and_conventions": "The exact excerpt is quoted above; the consumer Facts and proof step state the hypotheses and conventions used.",
          "supplier_proof_status": "Published mathematical result; current statement and proof carrier inspected.",
          "consumer_use": "F4 is used in step(s) 3.1, 3.2."
