          ]
        }
      ],
      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Let $m=\\|j-j'\\|_\\infty\\ge1$ for two distinct cube indices. In a coordinate\nwhere the index difference is $m$, the nearest points of the two intervals are\nseparated by $m(\\ell+g)-\\ell=(m-1)\\ell+mg\\ge mg$. Hence every pair of points\nin $C_j,C_{j'}$ has Euclidean distance at least $mg$.",
          "step": "1.1",
          "inputs": [
            "given",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-1-2",
          "claim": "For $m\\ge1$, [F3] gives the shell count. Use\n$x^d-y^d=(x-y)\\sum_{r=0}^{d-1}x^{d-1-r}y^r$ with $x=2m+1$, $y=2m-1$.\nSince $2m+1\\le3m$, it yields\n$$ (2m+1)^d-(2m-1)^d\\le2d(3m)^{d-1}=2d3^{d-1}m^{d-1}. $$\nTherefore $S_{d,\\epsilon}\\le2d3^{d-1}\\sum_{m\\ge1}m^{-1-\\epsilon}<\\infty$ by\n[F2], since $1+\\epsilon>1$.",
          "step": "1.2",
          "inputs": [
            "F2",
            "F3",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-2-1",
          "claim": "By [F1] and step 1.1, each such pair contributes at most\n$C(mg)^{-d-\\epsilon}$ in absolute value, because $mg\\ge g\\ge R$ and the\nEuclidean norm dominates the absolute value of any coordinate.",
          "step": "2.1",
          "inputs": [
            "F1",
            "step 1.1",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-3-1",
          "claim": "For a fixed cube $C_j$, sum step 2.1 over all other indices in $J$ and\nenlarge the finite set of index differences to all nonzero lattice vectors.\nBy [F3], grouping these vectors by $m=\\|k\\|_\\infty$ gives exactly the series\n$S_{d,\\epsilon}$ of the Statement, whose nonnegative sum is defined by [F2].\nthe result is at most $Cn^2S_{d,\\epsilon}g^{-d-\\epsilon}$. Summing this bound\nover the $M$ cubes counts each unordered pair twice, so dividing by $2$ gives\nthe claimed inequality.",
          "step": "3.1",
          "inputs": [
            "F2",
            "F3",
            "step 1.2",
            "step 2.1",
            "algebra"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "routine_steps": [],
      "boundaries": [
